  "description": "Audio: the bot speaks a TTS line into the room (long-running action with interim results), and audiohook - a separate connector - delivers a speaker-attributed audio segment.",
  "grounding": "v1 mic_audio.py plays WAVs to a virtual cable that Camfrog uses as its mic (resampled to 48 kHz). The audio worker waits up to 300 s for a free slot, posts a caption when playback starts (not before), and falls back to text when the mic stays full. transcriber.py records the room loopback, starts a segment on the first mic grab and ends it when the room's mic empties; holds over 300 s are chunked; one mixed stream, so overlap is attributed to the first holder; level stats (rms/peak/clip/tail dropout) feed automod's 'was the block warranted' check.",
